sentences.l:
He spoke, and to Patroclus with his brows he nodded in silence
for Phoenix to spread a solid bed, so that most quickly
out of the hut they might think of their homecoming;

and he does not turn to heed the friendship of his companions,
that with which beside the ships we honoured him above others,
pitiless one;

and he stays among the people, right there, having paid much,
but of the other are restrained the heart and manly spirit,
having accepted requital;

but for you an unrelenting and an evil
heart in your chest the gods have put, for the sake of one girl
alone;

for under your roof we are,
out of the throng of the Danaans, and we are eager, to you beyond others,
to be closest-tied and dearest, as many as are Achaeans.”

sentences.t:
εἴπ’ ἄγε μ’ ὦ πολύαιν’ Ὀδυσεῦ μέγα κῦδος Ἀχαιῶν
ἤ ῥ’ ἐθέλει νήεσσιν ἀλεξέμεναι δήϊον πῦρ,
ἦ ἀπέειπε, χόλος δ’ ἔτ’ ἔχει μεγαλήτορα θυμόν;

sentences.l:
And indeed to the others he said he would give counsel
to sail away home, since no longer will you find an end
of steep Ilios;

And Phoenix in turn, the old man, lay down, for so he bade,
so that with him in the ships to his dear fatherland he may follow
tomorrow, if he wishes;

“Atreus’-son, most glorious, lord of men, Agamemnon,
would that you had not besought the blameless son of Peleus,
giving countless gifts;
